{"skill":{"slug":"writing","displayName":"Writing"},"version":{"version":"1.1.2","createdAt":1785141257063,"changelog":"Clearer disclosure of what is stored and where","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":26411,"sha256":"a12c26808e755499b071db241cdfb9e1d24f9c77f96e0d496743c9827a083473","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":390,"sha256":"96fc9ba694f7c225e61811e8d011536904f51fe01677e430e0b1f23f171f58fd","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"clarity.md","size":10791,"sha256":"9a515fdec66d86c1f88b27f12705309c012a5d68a3edce634457ae6d195acc1f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"drafting.md","size":6893,"sha256":"c4cbf60cab6791cceb26a0179976abfa1770bb6988e8dadfa5204dd9ebf43a03","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"emails.md","size":10118,"sha256":"4d0a804656cdef716d952ab7f538b033511f4f864dfd47ad54c5e5d79e15313f","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"feedback.md","size":6379,"sha256":"e1bb9bf92d1da1fcd0b4a3fa312ecc12f7bb2e957d35891b6a36a6cde9b9506d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"memory-template.md","size":20954,"sha256":"1216377775b58f6774f2fb73966f59cd24cb358676bcb30cf8a5feed33ec546b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"posts.md","size":9569,"sha256":"6c264e985a0f5be49946d96418043deaae959ce1dfbf10f1495aaefec033eab0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"revision.md","size":7352,"sha256":"ac987479808fc9ce00ca9b793a778f9828ece16774c14871a0533f06353f509b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"second-language.md","size":7462,"sha256":"7ca6461ef7170c7ac50d7303609c870c05cc249b7c3bd8ab0444257661c342b4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"social.md","size":5912,"sha256":"71f4272815b3053ab0fcab52a59f258607c6e09fde6a370ac37c7c64ad192264","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"structure.md","size":9562,"sha256":"f9b53d90b289e927387a6de8dd2b5809857a094e75fd55b5e29ef1fef36d5b46","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"style-guide.md","size":6879,"sha256":"b872c5a6b6dafbad843a7a71f076c120b7486c9fd39fc6677a23cb27d5620161","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"voice.md","size":10013,"sha256":"0de1cb7a68ef30cce37f46e33d93b81712d1afb48490db3c1821cf5d673dd37e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"workplace.md","size":8873,"sha256":"b18be231e828cab812f04d573e9f37c96a516c68840d08eb65b46ab4cd1448b1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2063,"sha256":"e2d65f0f0a6d48243e301ce26ac18f371b13a06e489abaca8941fb77ce592d09","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789061029961,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"f437413cf51d4e372ee8fe508392bbdc84480ccaeb820f7ec3b14781e577343a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/f437413cf51d4e372ee8fe508392bbdc84480ccaeb820f7ec3b14781e577343a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1785147406997},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":38,"checkedAt":1789061029961},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a local writing assistant, but it automatically stores writing, contacts, and project notes without asking first, so it needs review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Access is scoped to declared local Clawic paths and the skill says no network requests or publishing, but it also uses shared contacts and projects files readable by other skills.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package inspected is markdown/json content only; I found no executable files, dependency install steps, shell hooks, or remote payload retrieval.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill has broad writing triggers and repeatedly instructs same-turn memory updates after ordinary writing, email, review, and workplace-document sessions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"artifact/memory-template.md explicitly says no permission is needed before writes, stores user prose samples and inferred preferences, updates shared contact/project records, and permits local moves/deletions inside the data area; this conflicts with the later privacy claim that drafts and pasted text are stored only when the user asks.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The drafting, editing, voice-matching, style-sheet, contact, and project-memory behavior mostly fits the stated purpose of learning and reusing a user's writing voice across sessions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a writing skill that keeps local long-term notes about your voice, samples, deadlines, contacts, and projects. Before using it on sensitive drafts or client work, pause recording or require the agent to ask before writing to ~/Clawic/data/, especially shared contacts and projects files.","findings":"[PE3] expected: The token and credential references are secret-redaction instructions, not evidence of credential theft; the artifact says credential values are not written and only pointers should be kept.\n[SDI-1] expected: Persistent writing memory is purpose-aligned for a voice-learning writing skill, but the automatic same-turn writes to memory, contacts, projects, style sheets, artifacts, and pieces create a material review concern.\n[SDI-2] expected: Cross-system writeback is disclosed and locally scoped, but the lack of per-write consent and use of shared stores make the behavior under-controlled for ordinary drafting tasks.\n[SQP-1] expected: The invocation scope is broad, but it is a general prose-writing skill with explicit exclusions for grammar-only, sales, academic, book, workflow, and inbox-management tasks.\n[RA2] expected: Cross-session memory is central to the stated purpose, yet the package stores sensitive writing traits, samples, contacts, deadlines, and project context by default.\n[SDI-4] expected: The clarity module's memory writes are part of the broader writing-memory design, not hidden code, but they extend a sentence-editing pass into persistent preference storage.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: The artifact-backed concern is valid: memory-template.md says no permission is needed, while several modules direct automatic writes of preferences, contact details, and project outcomes.\n[EA2] expected: The cited email and voice passages are drafting advice, not autonomous sending, destructive execution, or financial action; I did not find instructions to send messages or execute high-impact actions without user control.\n[SSD-3] expected: A shared writing profile is expected for the skill, but it may influence future sessions and expose context across skills without enough visibility or revocation controls beyond a paused status.\n[SQP-3] expected: The second-language guidance states that the user's audience decides the register, so the locale norm is contextual rather than a standalone security issue.\n[T09] expected: The static scan's automatic-persistence concern is supported by artifact text and is the main reason for the Review verdict, despite the absence of code execution or network behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789061029961}}}}}